                <head>277. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>On October 6, the North Atlantic Council met for discussions on Cyprus. The Greek
                    Representative informed the Council that his government would participate in a
                    conference on condition that its agenda include discussion of the ultimate
                    solution to the status of Cyprus. The British Representative indicated his
                    government’s willingness to participate in a conference. The Turkish
                    Representative also indicated his government’s willingness to participate but
                    rejected Spaak’s September 30 memorandum outlining terms of reference for the
                    meeting. Polto 885, October 6, reported on the meeting. (Department of State,
                    Central Files, 747C.00/10–658)</p>
            </div>
